From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm lanes: TF_GLM_OVN_NO_COPY, a DFlash2 drafter's windows without copied continuations

GLM's facts() leave the lanes core's copy_drafts at true, so a stream whose last tokens match
earlier context proposes a copied continuation, and that window replaces the block's held
drafts for the round. TF_GLM_OVN_NO_COPY (exactly 0 or 1, default off) has facts() set
copy_drafts = false when a DFlash2 drafter is loaded and the switch is on: the config's max_copy
is 0 and root and context copies are off, so no stream of the round proposes a copy and its
window carries the block's drafts. Off, or with no drafter, facts() are exactly as before.

One more effect of copy_drafts = false, from config.zig: first_copy becomes 1 and base_width 2, and base_width
sizes a window of forced tokens, so with the switch on a stream forces one token a round instead of up to three.
Forced tokens come only from a thinking block's close (a thinking budget's cut forces two of GLM's three close
tokens, a loop guard's close all three), and both happen only while thinking is open.

New here, not a re-seat: written on this series at v1.2.9. The row in
zig/src/platform/environment.zig sits after TF_GLM_OVN_WIN_FREE's and the line in
docs/environment.md after that switch's, so patches/pr1411's environment.zig and
docs/environment.md hunks still apply on top. no_copy_test.zig (the lanes core's GLM-shaped
lone stream, with and without the switch) and a facts() test in cuda_lanes_test.zig ride in
this patch.

Gates on pin+0001..0034: check-native-cuda-host and fmt green, test-cuda-host fails only the
base's own cli_config_test, lean 0 new; series and series+pr1411+cache-salt PASS against the
pristine base in the three-tree run.

